   "title": "How fire starts and spreads",
   "minutes": 8,
   "game": "Spread Sim",
   "html": "<h3>The fire triangle</h3>\n<p>A fire needs three things at the same time: <strong>heat</strong> (an ignition source), <strong>fuel</strong> (something that burns) and <strong>oxygen</strong> (usually from the air). Remove any one side of the triangle and the fire cannot start, or it goes out. Almost all fire prevention is about keeping heat and fuel apart.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Heat:</strong> faulty or overloaded electrics, heaters, cooking, smoking materials, hot work, friction, deliberate ignition.</li>\n<li><strong>Fuel:</strong> paper, cardboard, furniture, textiles, waste, flammable liquids and gases, plastics.</li>\n<li><strong>Oxygen:</strong> the air around us, plus oxygen cylinders and some chemicals that release oxygen.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>How fire spreads</h3>\n<p>Heat moves in three ways, and each one can carry a fire into new areas:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Convection:</strong> hot smoke and gases rise, spread along ceilings and travel up stairs, lift shafts and through gaps.</li>\n<li><strong>Conduction:</strong> heat passes through solid materials such as metal pipes, beams and walls, igniting things on the other side.</li>\n<li><strong>Radiation:</strong> heat travels through the air, like the warmth from a fire, and can ignite nearby items without touching them.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Fire also spreads by <strong>direct burning</strong>, as flames move from one item to the next. A small fire in a bin can involve a whole room in a few minutes.</p>\n\n<h3>Smoke is the real killer</h3>\n<p>Being overcome by smoke and toxic gases is the most common cause of death in fires, not burns. Smoke can contain carbon monoxide and other poisonous gases, it is very hot, and it quickly makes it impossible to see an exit sign a few metres away. A few breaths can disorientate you.</p>\n<p>This is why the rules focus on <strong>getting out early</strong> and <strong>keeping fire doors shut</strong>: a closed fire door holds back smoke and flames and protects the escape route.</p>\n\n<div class=\"callout\"><strong>Key point:</strong> fires grow fast and smoke travels further and faster than flames. Raise the alarm and get out early.</div>",
